---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import ConnectionStringParser from '../../components/ConnectionStringParser.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="Connection String Parser" description="Paste a database connection string and see its components broken out — host, port, database, credentials.">
  <ConnectionStringParser client:load slot="tool" />
  <h2>Debugging connection issues</h2>
  <p>When a connection fails, it's often faster to visually break the string into parts than to eyeball a long single-line URL for typos.</p>

  <h2>Common Connection String Parsing Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Missing URL-encoding in a manually written connection string</strong>, causing the parser to misinterpret special characters in the password or host.</li>
    <li><strong>Assuming a connection string works the same across drivers</strong> — some drivers accept extra query parameters others don't recognize.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to Use This Connection String Parser</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Debugging a failing database connection by inspecting its parsed components</li>
    <li>Verifying a connection string was constructed correctly before deploying</li>
    <li>Understanding an unfamiliar connection string shared by a teammate</li>
  </ul>
</ToolLayout>
